## Why This Is Asked
Designing a versioning layer tests understanding of prompt drift, fallback logic, and observability in prompts.

## Key Concepts
- Versioned prompts, fallback strategies
- Signals: intent, confidence, version_stability
- Edge cases: outdated version, conflicting signals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal version routing prototype
function routePrompt(prompt, version, scores) {
  const versions = ['v1','v2','v3'];
  let chosen = version && versions.includes(version) ? version : versions
    .map((v,i)=>({v, s: (scores && scores[i]) || 0}))
    .sort((a,b)=> b.s - a.s)
    [0].v;

  // Fallback logic for edge cases
  if (scores[chosen] < threshold || isOutdated(chosen)) {
    chosen = findMostStableVersion(versions, chosen);
    logFallback(chosen, prompt, scores);
  }

  return {
    version: chosen,
    plan: generatePlan(prompt, chosen),
    payload: buildPayload(prompt, chosen)
  };
}
```

